"Software" means qorc, including its source code, documentation, assets, and other materials distributed by the copyright holder under this License.

"Original Software" means the qorc software as distributed by the copyright holder.

"Modified Version" means any version of the Software that has been changed, extended, adapted, translated, or otherwise derived from the Software.

"Non-Commercial" means use that is not intended or reasonably expected to generate revenue, financial gain, commercial advantage, or monetary compensation, directly or indirectly.

2. Copyright

The Software is copyrighted by its original copyright holder.

This License does not transfer ownership of the Software or its copyright to any recipient.

You may not claim ownership of the original qorc source code or represent yourself as the original creator or copyright holder of qorc.

You may retain copyright notices identifying your own original contributions to a Modified Version, but you must preserve all copyright notices relating to qorc and its original author.

3. Permission to Use

Permission is granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of the Software to:

- Use the Software for Non-Commercial purposes.
- Study and inspect the source code.
- Modify the Software.
- Create Modified Versions.
- Compile and run Modified Versions.
- Make private modifications without publishing those modifications.
- Share the Software or Modified Versions for Non-Commercial purposes, subject to the conditions of this License.

4. Non-Commercial Requirement

The Software and all Modified Versions may only be used, distributed, modified, hosted, or otherwise provided for Non-Commercial purposes.

You may not:

- Sell the Software.
- Sell a Modified Version.
- Charge money for access to the Software or a Modified Version.
- Offer the Software or a Modified Version as a paid service.
- Use the Software or a Modified Version to provide a commercial service.
- Monetize the Software or a Modified Version through subscriptions, licensing fees, paid downloads, paid hosting, advertisements, sponsorships, donations tied to access, or substantially similar methods.
- Incorporate the Software or a Modified Version into a commercial product or service.
- Use the Software or a Modified Version primarily to obtain commercial advantage or monetary compensation.

Commercial use requires separate written permission from the copyright holder.

5. Copyleft — Same License Requirement

Any Modified Version that is distributed, published, or otherwise made available to another person must be distributed under this exact License.

You may not place a different license on a Modified Version.

You may not distribute a Modified Version under a proprietary, closed-source, commercial, permissive, or otherwise incompatible license.

You must provide recipients of a Modified Version with:

1. The complete corresponding source code of the Modified Version; and
2. A copy of this License.

Recipients must receive the same rights and restrictions granted by this License.

You may not impose additional restrictions that prevent recipients from exercising the rights granted by this License.

6. Source Code

When distributing the Software or a Modified Version, you must provide the corresponding source code or provide a clear and reasonable method for recipients to obtain the complete corresponding source code.

The source code must include your modifications necessary to reproduce the distributed version.

You may not distribute a compiled or packaged version while intentionally withholding the corresponding source code.

7. Attribution

All distributions of the Software or Modified Versions must retain:

- The original qorc copyright notice.
- This License.
- Existing attribution notices.
- Existing license notices.

You must not remove or obscure attribution to qorc or its original author.

If you create a Modified Version, you may identify yourself as the author of your modifications, but you must clearly distinguish your contributions from the original qorc work.

For example:

«Based on qorc, originally created by the qorc copyright holder.
Modified by [Your Name].»

You may not state or imply that you originally created qorc.

8. Name, Branding, and Trademarks

This License does not grant permission to use the qorc name, logo, trademarks, service marks, domain names, or other branding to imply that a Modified Version is the official qorc project.

Modified Versions must not falsely represent themselves as the official qorc software.

You may state that your project is "based on qorc" provided that the statement is truthful and does not imply endorsement or official affiliation.

9. Private Modifications

You may modify the Software for private use without publishing or distributing your modifications.

Private modifications do not have to be disclosed to the copyright holder.

However, if you distribute or otherwise make a Modified Version available to another person, the requirements of Sections 5, 6, and 7 apply.

10. No Sublicensing

You may not sublicense the Software or grant another person rights that are broader than those provided by this License.

Every recipient must receive the Software under this License.

You may not remove the Non-Commercial or Copyleft requirements.

11. Commercial Licensing

The copyright holder may separately grant commercial licenses or additional permissions to individuals or organizations.

A commercial license must be explicitly granted in writing by the copyright holder.

Receiving the Software under this License does not grant any commercial rights.

The copyright holder retains the exclusive right to commercially license the Software, subject to the rights granted by this License for previously distributed versions.

12. Contributions

Unless a separate written agreement states otherwise, contributors retain copyright in their original contributions.

Contributors must have the necessary rights to submit their contributions.

Contributions incorporated into qorc may be distributed as part of the Software under this License.

13. Termination

Any rights granted under this License terminate automatically if you violate its terms.

Upon termination, you must cease distribution and use of the Software or Modified Version to the extent required by applicable law.

Rights may be reinstated at the sole discretion of the copyright holder through written permission.

14. No Warranty

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED.

TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, THE COPYRIGHT HOLDER SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, OR OTHER LIABILITY ARISING FROM THE USE OF OR INABILITY TO USE THE SOFTWARE.

15. Acceptance

By using, modifying, distributing, or otherwise exercising rights granted by this License, you agree to be bound by its terms.

If you do not agree to these terms, you may not use, modify, distribute, or otherwise exercise rights granted by this License.

